this was the 25th pride march in  budapest but the event was as much about  protest  as celebration the target this man  prime minister viktor orban and his new  rules restricting the promotion of  lgbt plus rights what he calls  homosexual propaganda  he's been widely condemned and some  european politicians traveled  here to register their discontent  orbin is only on he's just starting  you know he's built a foundation that he  can stand on  um and then we're gonna start seeing  more and more rollbacks of rights and  then how can i wear a european uh mask  or flag and say  everybody's equal because that's not the  case the british embassy handed these  out declaring love is great with a  rainbow version of the union flag you  saw them everywhere  it was a march that was generally joyous  and loud  many came with children even though  bringing them here might now be  illegal so was this about putting  pressure on mr orban  can be can be a message but i don't  think so he's  care about this message unfortunately  he's not listening  no the turnout big the policing  restrained  but this raucous celebration masks a  schism in hungarian society  lgbt plus rights is a divisive issue  here  what's happening here is that people on  the pride march are having their photos  taken  with this as a backdrop that's the  counter demonstration  by those who think that the lgbt plus  community  are poisoning hungarian culture  when we spoke to them divided from the  march by metal gate  they were vociferous smaller number but  loud and belligerent  if somebody is gay i i don't  do anything but i am against the person  who is  doing gay propaganda against the  children  in the school in the kindergarten that's  what we are against not the gay person  i feel sorry for them and some of these  messages were about  driving lgbt plus people out of hungary  and the cruel irony is that these new  laws the sense of being under attack  are leading some people here to consider  abandoning their country  if i imagine myself in five or ten years  living here  and getting all this hate getting all  this negative environment  we are just very sad about them and we  are just planning to leave the country  as soon as possible  it is a year until hungary's next  general election if mr orban earns a  fourth consecutive victory  budapest pride could end up feeling very  different  adam parsons sky news budapest
 

